# GC-P17 container proof -- Alpine runtime image, real agent against the demo device,
# delivered to two local sinks. No real terminal, no BC, no ingest deployment.
#
# Generated by the GC-P17 worker on an Apple Silicon dev host running Linux containers
# (Alpine / aarch64). Every address in this file is loopback; every record is the repo's
# own synthetic demo fixture (demo_device.DemoDevice). Nothing here names a real device,
# tenant, host or credential.
#
# What this proves that the unit suite cannot: that the shipped image starts, runs the
# real `agent_cli.SiteAgent.tick()` on a loopback ISAPI device, stores, queues and
# DELIVERS to both sinks -- as the unprivileged image user, on a read-only root
# filesystem, with the scratch tree on a tmpfs.
#
# Commands, verbatim (from the repo root, on the branch tip under test):
#
#   docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile -t gateclerk-agent:local .
#   docker build -f "$TMPDIR/gc-p17/Dockerfile" -t gateclerk-agent:gc17 .
#   docker run --rm --read-only --tmpfs /tmp:rw,size=64m \
#     gateclerk-agent:gc17 \
#     demo demo --root /tmp/gc17-demo --ticks 2 --keep -o json
#
# `gateclerk-agent:gc17` is a disposable layer on top of the built image, created and
# thrown away inside this proof; `deploy/Dockerfile` is unchanged (see section [2]).
# The demo run passed no --user flag: the image's own USER is what ran.

