### [9b] reading the two lines a reviewer will stop at
  - the clock_skew warning: by fixture design. demo_device.py:42 documents that the
    fake claims +02:00 year-round inside a Europe/Bucharest site, so its claimed wall
    time sits a fixed 35760 s off on every run of this deterministic demo. GC-P04's
    skew channel reports it as a warning; the tick still came back ok and both sinks
    still drained (pushed 24 of 24, dead_lettered 0) -- the agent reads the skew, warns,
    and never writes the device clock.
  - sinks.*.pushed is the FOLD of both ticks (demo_walkthrough._sum_sink_counts
    collapses SiteTickReport.sinks into one total per sink); ticks=2 in section [8] is
    what it is folded over. csv.rows is the row count in the delivered file.

